  "design": {
    "fork": "The version-matched zygote native fork marks only the system-server child. No JNI, allocations or threads run in the ART fork region.",
    "initialization": "The replacement nativeZygoteInit first performs the original AndroidRuntime::onZygoteInit virtual call. Only the marked child, with the explicit service environment flag, starts the bridge.",
    "context": "A daemon waits for the existing ActivityThread system context and sys.boot_completed; it never calls systemMain again. The existing InputManager and host NetworkAgent implementation are reused.",
    "endpoint": "The system role binds its filesystem socket after fork, avoiding inheritance in zygote/app children. Unexpected non-socket entries are rejected; stale socket entries are removed.",
    "authentication": "Original kernel PID/UID and open host proc-stat descriptor/start-time checks remain. Logical guest roles are metadata and do not provide kernel isolation.",
    "readiness": "The bridge publishes readiness into the inherited boot console as well as Java logging, since ZygoteInit routes Java streams to liblog.",
    "failure": "Failure of the critical embedded input bridge requests a clean whole-guest stop. Network bootstrap errors retain their previous input-independent handling."
  },
